X:1
T:All Praise To Thee, My God, This Night
T:TALLIS CANON
C:Music: Thomas Tallis, circa 1567 · Words: Thomas Ken, circa 1674
S:Open Hymnal Project ABC (openhymnal.org; marked public domain), melody line with every stanza as printed there; their source: Episcopal Hymnal, 1916 Hymn 25.. Melody cross-checked against the hymnary.org score (hymnary.org/tune/tallis_canon): 100% of pitches and 100% of note lengths agree.
M:4/4
L:1/4
Q:1/4=100
K:G
G | G F G G | A A B G | c c B B | A A G
w: All praise to Thee, my God, this night, For all the bless- ings of the light!
w: For- give me, Lord, for Thy dear Son, The ill that I this day have done,
w: Teach me to live, that I may dread The grave as lit- tle as my bed.
w: O may my soul on Thee re- pose, And with sweet sleep mine eye- lids close,
w: When in the night I sleep- less lie, My soul with heav'n- ly thoughts sup- ply;
w: O when shall I, in end- less day, For ev- er chase dark sleep a- way,
w: Praise God, from Whom all bles- sings flow; Praise Him, all crea- tures here be- low;
d | c A B B | A A G D | E F G B | A A G |]
w: Keep me, O keep me, King of kings, Be- neath Thine own al- migh- ty wings.
w: That with the world, my- self, and Thee, I, ere I sleep, at peace may be.
w: Teach me to die, that so I may Rise glo- rious at the judg- ment day.
w: Sleep that may me more vig- 'rous make To serve my God when I a- wake.
w: Let no ill dreams dis- turb my rest, No pow'rs of dark- ness me mo- lest.
w: And hymns di- vine with an- gels sing, All praise to thee, e- ter- nal King?
w: Praise Him a- bove, ye heav'n- ly host; Praise Fa- ther, Son, and Ho- ly Ghost.
